<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hamdullahi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1820–1864</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hamdullahi, the House of Praise, was the capital of the Massina Empire in the inner <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> delta of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>. It was founded around 1820 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seku-amadu">Seku Amadu</a> after his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a> against the Fulbe chiefs and their Bambara overlords, and was laid out as a planned Islamic city with a great mosque and a ruling council. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-hadj-umar-tall">El Hadj Umar Tall</a> captured it in 1862, and it was ruined in the fighting of 1864.</p></div>
